  "chapterId": "puc2-maths-08-application-of-integrals",
  "topicId": "puc2-maths-08-application-of-integrals.t1",
  "stem": {
   "en": "The area bounded by y = cos x and the x-axis between x = 0 and x = π is:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "0"
   },
   {
    "en": "1 sq. unit"
   },
   {
    "en": "π sq. units"
   },
   {
    "en": "2 sq. units"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 3,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "cos x is positive on (0, π/2) and negative on (π/2, π). Area = ∫₀^{π/2} cos x dx + |∫_{π/2}^{π} cos x dx| = 1 + 1 = 2. The plain integral from 0 to π gives 0, which is not the area."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC",
   "KCET",
   "COMEDK",
   "JEE"
  ],
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "tags": []
